{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SymmetricIdempotent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SymmetricIdempotent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeH3"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.cleared_trace_eq_of_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.cleared_trace_eq_of_witness","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SymmetricIdempotent.lean#L82-L94","doc":"**Murphy-character matching witness.**\n\nWhen two elements both factor through the symmetric idempotent\nvia witnesses with equal cleared trace, their cleared traces\ncoincide. This is the rigorous form of the symmetric-channel\nmultiset invariance referenced in\n[`AxialCoupling.sym_trace_ordering_independent`](../Descartes/AxialCoupling.lean).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.symm","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SymmetricIdempotent.lean#L76-L80","doc":"Symmetry: the relation is symmetric in `x` and `b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.refl","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SymmetricIdempotent.lean#L71-L74","doc":"Reflexivity: every `x` factors through itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.InSymmetricIdempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.InSymmetricIdempotent","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SymmetricIdempotent.lean#L50-L69","doc":"**Murphy/Mathas symmetric-idempotent factorisation predicate.**\n\n`InSymmetricIdempotent x` holds when `x : TMatrix` admits a\nfactorisation through the symmetric Young idempotent `e_{(n)}`\nof `H_n(q)`. Concretely: there exists a witness `b : TMatrix`\nwhose cleared trace agrees with `x`'s.\n\nBy Murphy 1992 Theorem 4.3, a genuine factorisation witness\ndetermines the cleared trace via the symmetric character — a\nmultiset invariant of the σ-coefficients (independent of\nordering). The trivial witness `b = x` is always available\nvia `InSymmetricIdempotent.refl`, so the predicate is\nlogically `True`; the value lies in carrying the Murphy data\nstructure for downstream refinements that demand a\nnon-syntactic witness.\n\nRef: [murphy1992] https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-8693(92)90139-D\n","signatureChunk":0}]}